---
arrangement-when-used: `dorc why <book.sh:N> --last` over a durable whose recorded book digest no longer matches the file at the recorded path. The reader asked about a LINE; the run's line numbers belong to bytes this durable never carried, so the whole answer is this one row.
arrangement-why: 28F rul-drift-replay-d1 + 271 rul-sin-ordering — naming a line here would be a mis-attribution (pope-sin), which is worse than a missing answer. No banner and no footer either: the banner answers about the run, and the footer claims a selection nothing here selected.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# The book AS IT IS NOW — not the bytes the durable below was keyed on. Line 5 exists in THIS
# file; whether it existed in the analyzed one is exactly what nobody can say.
apt-get install -y nginx
systemctl enable nginx

-- .whylog --
dorc-whylog/2 nonce=dorc attempt=0 host=web1 target=width-one generation=width-one mode=whylog-replay started=1784944837000 @@dorc@@
book digest=aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa path=book.sh @@dorc@@
argv value=dorc @@dorc@@
argv value=plan @@dorc@@
argv value=book.sh @@dorc@@
digest decision=bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb @@dorc@@
apply leaf=0 disposition=run predicted=1 @@dorc@@
apply leaf=1 disposition=guard predicted=1 @@dorc@@
results bytes=0 @@dorc@@
dorc-whylog-end/2 @@dorc@@

-- replay --
$ dorc why book.sh:5 --last --whylog=.whylog
[unwritten: why-drift-address-unanswerable]
